nfs-ganesha (15.10-1+ezgh5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0002: addrs.<nodeid> starts with "host <hostname>" and "pid <pid>"
    lines, so a fencer can tell this instance from a replacement; no address
    from rados_getaddrs() fails startup instead of writing "(null)"; once it
    is published the RADOS URLs module creates no new client (a reread that
    needs one is refused) and keeps the one it has on a failed ioctx create.
  * d/p/0003: grace-db notifies wait 1 s, not 500 ms, which librados rounds
    to 0 s and the OSD then treats as its 30 s default; the RECLAIM_COMPLETE
    path reads the client count without the grace lock.

 -- EZGH Cloud <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000

nfs-ganesha (15.10-1+ezgh4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0002-rados_cluster-publish-this-instance-s-RADOS-client-addresses.patch:
    the rados_cluster recovery backend writes addrs.<nodeid> ("recov <addr>"
    and, with RADOS URLs, "urls <addr>", from rados_getaddrs()) in the grace
    database's pool and namespace before it touches the grace database, and
    ganesha.nfsd exits if it can't, so a takeover can blocklist them.
  * d/p/0003-grace-shorter-grace-db-notifies-lift-as-soon-as-reclaim-is-complete.patch:
    grace-database notifies wait 500 ms for acks, not 3 s; the reaper is woken
    when the last expected client sends RECLAIM_COMPLETE.

 -- EZGH Cloud <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

nfs-ganesha (15.10-1+ezgh3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0001-tls-fail-startup-on-a-bad-certificate-and-reload-it-on-SIGHUP.patch:
    - A CA file that doesn't load (TLS_CA_File unset and nothing at the
      default /etc/ganesha/tls/ca.crt) no longer stops startup: no client
      certificate is requested then. Only the certificate and key must load.
    - SIGHUP rereads TLS_CONFIG before the LOG and EXPORT blocks, so a bad
      export can't hold back a renewal, and reloads only when the
      certificate, key or CA file changed; a failed load or a TLS on/off
      change is logged once.
    - The credential swap takes a plain mutex instead of a rwlock.

 -- EZGH Cloud <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000

nfs-ganesha (15.10-1+ezgh2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0001-tls-fail-startup-on-a-bad-certificate-and-reload-it-on-SIGHUP.patch:
    ganesha.nfsd exits at startup when TLS_CONFIG enables TLS and its
    certificate or key fails to load; SIGHUP rereads TLS_CONFIG and swaps a
    freshly loaded certificate in for new connections (established sessions
    keep theirs; a failed load keeps the current one).
  * nfs-ganesha-ceph and nfs-ganesha-rados-grace depend on libcephfs2 and
    librados2 at exactly 20.2.4-1noble: libcephfs2 needs libceph-common's
    private symbols from the same librados2 build.
  * nfs-ganesha depends on libtirpc-common: ntirpc reads /etc/netconfig and
    ganesha.nfsd exits at startup without it.

 -- EZGH Cloud <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

